1. Introduction
1.1 Purpose
This SRS defines functional and non-functional requirements for CinemaVision Pro based on the current implemented codebase (frontend + backend monorepo).

1.2 Scope
CinemaVision Pro is a full-stack web app for movie browsing, showtime lookup, seat selection, booking, and admin management.

Implemented highlights:
- JWT authentication and role-based authorization.
- Movie/theater/showtime CRUD (admin).
- Booking lifecycle: create, list, cancel, delete (cancelled only).
- Forgot/reset password via email token.
- EN/VI locale support and VND/USD currency display.
- Frontend payment simulation (ATM/Momo/ZaloPay/VNPay UI).

2. Overall Description
2.1 User Classes
- Visitor (unauthenticated)
- Registered User (authenticated)
- Administrator (role=admin)

2.2 Operating Environment
- Frontend: React + TypeScript + Vite
- Backend: Express + MongoDB (Mongoose)
- Runtime: Node.js, npm workspaces

2.3 Constraints
- Password hashed with bcryptjs.
- JWT required for protected APIs.
- Admin routes require admin role.
- API security middleware: helmet, cors, express-rate-limit.

3. Functional Requirements
3.1 Visitor Requirements
FR-V-1: Visitor can browse movies and view details.
FR-V-2: Visitor can search/filter movies via movie search API.
FR-V-3: Visitor can browse theaters by region and view showtimes.
FR-V-4: Visitor can register account and login.
FR-V-5: Visitor can request forgot password and use reset link.

3.2 Registered User Requirements
FR-U-1: User can view/update profile.
FR-U-2: User can change password.
FR-U-3: User can select seats and create booking.
FR-U-4: User can view own bookings.
FR-U-5: User can cancel own booking.
FR-U-6: User can delete own cancelled booking.

3.3 Admin Requirements
FR-A-1: Admin can manage movies (CRUD).
FR-A-2: Admin can manage theaters (CRUD).
FR-A-3: Admin can manage showtimes (CRUD).
FR-A-4: Admin can view all users and update roles.
FR-A-5: Admin cannot self-demote from admin to user.
FR-A-6: Admin cannot delete own account.
FR-A-7: Admin can view all bookings and update booking status (confirmed/cancelled).
FR-A-8: Admin can view dashboard statistics.

3.4 Booking Rules (Implemented)
BR-1: Booking creation requires valid JWT.
BR-2: Backend validates showtime existence.
BR-3: Backend checks availableSeats >= selected seats.
BR-4: Backend rejects seat conflicts against confirmed bookings in same showtime.
BR-5: Backend computes totalPrice as seatCount * showtime.price.
BR-6: Backend generates unique bookingReference and retries on duplicate collision.
BR-7: On successful booking, availableSeats is decremented.
BR-8: On cancel booking, availableSeats is incremented.
BR-9: User can only cancel/delete own booking.
BR-10: Only cancelled bookings can be deleted.

4. External Interface Requirements
4.1 Main API Endpoints (Aligned)
Authentication:
- POST /api/auth/register
- POST /api/auth/login
- GET /api/auth/profile
- PUT /api/auth/profile
- PUT /api/auth/change-password
- POST /api/auth/forgot-password
- POST /api/auth/reset-password/:token

Movies:
- GET /api/movies
- GET /api/movies/search
- GET /api/movies/:id
- POST /api/movies (admin)
- PUT /api/movies/:id (admin)
- DELETE /api/movies/:id (admin)

Theaters:
- GET /api/theaters
- GET /api/theaters/regions
- GET /api/theaters/region/:region
- GET /api/theaters/:id
- GET /api/theaters/:theaterId/movies
- GET /api/theaters/:theaterId/movies/:movieId/showtimes
- POST /api/theaters (admin)
- PUT /api/theaters/:id (admin)
- DELETE /api/theaters/:id (admin)

Showtimes:
- GET /api/showtimes
- GET /api/showtimes/:id
- GET /api/showtimes/movie/:movieId
- GET /api/showtimes/theater/:theaterId
- POST /api/showtimes (admin)
- PUT /api/showtimes/:id (admin)
- DELETE /api/showtimes/:id (admin)

Bookings:
- GET /api/bookings (own bookings, auth)
- POST /api/bookings (auth)
- PUT /api/bookings/:id/cancel (auth)
- DELETE /api/bookings/:id (auth, cancelled only)
- GET /api/bookings/showtime/:showtimeId/booked-seats (public)

Admin:
- GET /api/admin/stats
- GET /api/admin/users
- PUT /api/admin/users/:userId/role
- DELETE /api/admin/users/:userId
- GET /api/admin/bookings
- PUT /api/admin/bookings/:bookingId/status

System:
- GET /api/health

5. Quality Attributes
5.1 Security
- JWT auth for protected routes.
- Role-based access for admin routes.
- Password hashing with bcryptjs.
- Forgot-password token stored hashed with 1-hour expiry.
- Generic forgot-password response to avoid account enumeration.

5.2 Performance and Reliability
- Rate limiting: 1000 requests/IP/15 minutes.
- Graceful error handling and 404 handling.
- Booking flow includes conflict checks to avoid duplicate seat confirmation.

5.3 Usability
- Responsive UI for desktop/mobile.
- Custom frontend 404 page.
- Locale switch EN/VI and currency display VND/USD.

6. Known Gaps / Planned Future Scope
- Current payment is simulated on frontend; real payment gateway/webhook validation is future scope.
- No WebSocket-based seat locking in current release.
- No booking confirmation email in current release (email currently used for password reset only).

7. Traceability to Code
- Auth/Profile: backend/server/controllers/authController.js, backend/server/middleware/auth.js, frontend/src/lib/auth.tsx
- Booking: backend/server/controllers/bookingController.js, backend/server/routes/bookings.js, backend/server/models/Booking.js
- Admin: backend/server/routes/adminRoutes.js, backend/server/controllers/adminController.js
- Movies/Theaters/Showtimes: backend/server/routes/*.js and corresponding controllers/models
- Frontend protected UI: frontend/src/components/ProtectedRoute.tsx

